>making.  How would you conduct the Nation's business?  I presume that you
>do not seek a personal veto power over public decisions? 

Why would you presume not? That is exactly what we seek. Personal
sovereignty. Minimal to non-existant government by informed contract
among peers.

Democracy is mob rule, and the noble attempt to contain it in a
Republican constitution in the USA is up in smoke. "It only required
150 years to get from a Constitution that reserved all rights to
the states and the people not delegated to the government, to a
Supreme Court willing to rule that growing corn on your own land
